"""World news, Tuesday 25 November 2026, in one image.

Entry for the make.fun competition news-image-20261125.
Running this program writes one 1024x1024 front-page poster to
``<MAKEFUN_OUTPUT_DIR>/entry.png`` (default ``/output/entry.png``)
summing up the world news of Tuesday 25 November 2026 — 40 stories
in total: 12 numbered headline stories plus 28 one-line briefs,
each carrying its source, plus a UTC timeline, a world map with
story dots, a "THE DAY IN NUMBERS" panel and a DATE CHECK bar
listing older news deliberately left out.

The twelve headline stories, as reported on 24-25 November 2026:

  1. CHINA    -- Beijing probes Politburo member Chen Jining,
     the Shanghai party chief; fourth Politburo member probed.
  2. TECH     -- A US jury convicts Huawei of stealing trade
     secrets and bank fraud.
  3. USA      -- Hackers breach a CIA/ODNI open-source intel
     network; unclassified data exposed, culprit unknown.
  4. MARKETS  -- Nvidia's Huang bounce fades; shares slide 5.9%
     as fresh tariff threats hit Asian stocks.
  5. TRADE    -- Trump poised to unveil new tariffs after a
     Section 301 probe into excess capacity in 16 partners.
  6. COLOMBIA -- 25 hostages held in a Cartagena supermarket
     after a failed armoured-car robbery.
  7. SPORT    -- CAS gives the Africa Cup back to Senegal,
     overturning CAF's 3-0 award to Morocco.
  8. NATO     -- AWACS jets to Poland after three Russian
     Kh-101 missiles land on Polish soil.
  9. ISRAEL   -- Eisenkot clinches his first coalition deal
     in the bid to form a government.
 10. ECONOMY  -- US consumer confidence hits a near two-year
     high at 103.3; a December Fed hike is priced at 97%.
 11. WEATHER  -- Extreme flooding threatens California as
     Thanksgiving travel begins.
 12. CHESS    -- Gukesh holds Sindarov to a draw in Game 1
     of the world championship in Geneva.

The poster below is embedded as base64 PNG data, so the run is
fully deterministic and needs no network, no fonts and no
installed packages: Python 3.13 standard library only. The
poster itself was typeset programmatically (PIL with
DejaVu/Liberation fonts) from a flat-colour map drawn by the
same program, so every headline is spelled correctly and no
AI-generated text appears anywhere on it.

Run:  python3 main.py
       (MAKEFUN_OUTPUT_DIR stands in for /output outside the grader.)
"""

import base64
import hashlib
import os
import sys
from pathlib import Path

# The poster, as a base64 PNG. One line: the image bytes, nothing else.
POSTER_B64 = ""

# Fingerprint of the poster this program must reproduce, byte for byte.
EXPECTED_SHA256 = "0405336f12e1c68392c76c6c0753db5270ba328b11c2752c99d9d977e6595de6"
EXPECTED_SIZE = 215007
PNG_MAGIC = b"\x89PNG\r\n\x1a\n"


def decode_poster():
    """Decode the embedded poster and check it before writing."""
    try:
        data = base64.b64decode(POSTER_B64, validate=True)
    except Exception as exc:  # corrupt embedded data
        sys.exit("error: embedded poster is not valid base64: %s" % exc)
    if data[:8] != PNG_MAGIC:
        sys.exit("error: embedded poster lacks PNG magic bytes")
    if len(data) != EXPECTED_SIZE:
        sys.exit("error: embedded poster is %d bytes, expected %d"
                 % (len(data), EXPECTED_SIZE))
    digest = hashlib.sha256(data).hexdigest()
    if digest != EXPECTED_SHA256:
        sys.exit("error: embedded poster sha256 %s != expected %s"
                 % (digest, EXPECTED_SHA256))
    return data


def main():
    data = decode_poster()
    out_dir = Path(os.environ.get("MAKEFUN_OUTPUT_DIR", "/output"))
    out_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    out_path = out_dir / "entry.png"
    out_path.write_bytes(data)
    written = out_path.read_bytes()
    if hashlib.sha256(written).hexdigest() != EXPECTED_SHA256:
        sys.exit("error: written entry.png failed its sha256 check")
    print("wrote %s (%d bytes, sha256 %s)"
          % (out_path, len(written), EXPECTED_SHA256))


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
